permitted to socially interact with unmarried men. Court ships between young couples were strictly controlled by their families, and in Seraphina Lococco's case, her father did not like Pietro Santoro. Without his approval, there would be no marriage. One day in the summer of 1962, Pietro and Seraphina performed what was known as a fuetina, an elopement of sorts. They spent a week together hidden in the countryside, and upon her return home, Seraphina informed her father that she was now a dishonoured woman.
允许与未婚男子进行社交互动。年轻情侣之间的求爱受到家庭的严格控制，而在塞拉菲娜·洛科科的案例中，她的父亲不喜欢彼得罗·桑托罗。没有他的批准，就不会有婚姻。1962 年夏天的一天，彼得罗和塞拉菲娜上演了所谓的“私奔”（fuetina）。他们在乡村躲藏了一周，回到家后，塞拉菲娜告诉父亲，她现在是一个名誉扫地的女人了。

